@{comment: Deep Relaxation — 10 min session example}
@{voice: en_US-amy-medium}
@{speed: 0.85}
@{section: Introduction}

Welcome to this guided relaxation session, {{name}}.
Find a comfortable position, and when you are ready, gently close your eyes.

@{pause: 5s}

Take a slow, deep breath in through your nose.

@{pause: 4s}

And breathe out slowly through your mouth.

@{pause: 4s}

@{section: Body Scan}

Now bring your awareness to your feet and ankles.
Notice any tension you might be holding there.

@{pause: 4s}

As you breathe out, let that tension dissolve completely.
Feel your feet becoming heavy and warm.

@{pause: 6s}

Moving upward now, to your calves and your shins.
Allow these muscles to soften and release.

@{pause: 6s}

Continue upward to your thighs and your hips.
With every breath, you sink a little deeper into relaxation.

@{pause: 8s}

@{section: Deepening}
@{speed: 0.80}

With each breath you take, you drift further and further.
Every sound you hear only takes you deeper into this peaceful state.

@{pause: 10s}

You are completely safe. Completely at ease.
Nothing can disturb you here, {{name}}.

@{pause: 15s}

@{section: Awakening}
@{speed: 0.90}

In a moment, I will count from one to five.
With each number, you will feel more alert and refreshed.

@{pause: 3s}

One. Becoming aware of your surroundings.

@{pause: 3s}

Two. Feeling energy gently returning to your body.

@{pause: 3s}

Three. Taking a deep, refreshing breath.

@{pause: 3s}

Four. Almost fully awake now.

@{pause: 3s}

Five. Eyes open. Fully alert. Feeling wonderful.

@{pause: 2s}

Welcome back, {{name}}. Take a moment before you continue with your day.
engines.